{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.domain`\n\nThe {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`trust_but_verify::domain::Domain` to define its node-identity type. Its\nerror type is introduced in {cite}`requirements.sdk.errors`:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n\n    /// The *identifier* identifies a particular node in the graph.\n    type NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.graph.domain_types` has one obligation. The application domain implements `Domain` and defines `NodeId` with the bounds `Clone + Eq + Send + Sync`. The wording leaves nothing ambiguous.\n\n**Declared bound (not loosened).**\n- In `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]`, the nested `check_bounds<G: Domain>` calls `identity::<G::NodeId>()`.\n- That helper requires `T: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync`. The call compiles only if `Domain::NodeId` guarantees every one of those bounds. Dropping any bound from the trait would break compilation of this test.\n\n**Declared bound (not tightened).**\n- The test's `Identity` fixture is `Clone + PartialEq + Eq`, and its only field is a `u8`, so it is also `Send + Sync`. It deliberately has no `Debug`, `Hash`, `Ord` or `Default`.\n- `check_bounds::<Relationships>()` and the `Domain` impl compile only if `NodeId` demands no more than the required bounds. Adding any extra bound to `NodeId` would fail to compile.\n\n**Implementations defining `NodeId`.** Several tests implement `Domain` with their own `NodeId` and use it in real operations:\n- `contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` uses the opaque `Identity` in node reads, `load_evidence`, `store_evidence`, `node_path` and `outgoing_edges`.\n- `tests/validation.rs#fn[enum_node_ids_distinguish_requirements_and_source_items_in_one_domain]` uses an enum `ReviewNodeId`. It asserts `assert_ne!` on distinct ids, runs `node_path`, `outgoing_edges`, reads, and evidence store and load keyed by id.\n- The Habeas domain tests in `src/sdk.rs` and `src/authoring/sdk.rs` cover `HabeasNode` as a `NodeId`. They check path distinctness, equality across reconstructed domains, and edges.\n- The `agent/tests.rs` tests cover `Node` ids in validation and agent flows.\n\nTogether these exercise `Eq` and `Clone` on real ids and cover the \"define its node-identity type\" part.\n\n**Gaps.** None found. The `Send + Sync` bound is checked at compile time through the generic helper, and nothing else in the requirement needs runtime assertions.",
  "references": "2e0816c1915fe94d28b5451c052712a0824feb8e7d2babaf5a1c18a378452fcc",
